    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i get the privacy argument, but honestly it feels like a lot of these fears are being used to block tech that could actually save lives. isn't the reality that if we just have better tech, we can catch criminals way faster and make the city safer for everyone? does the risk of a few false positives really outweigh the benefit of preventing major crimes?",
